{"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/ConsoleDestination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InvalidCapacity"],"title":"Destinations","anchor":"Destinations"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/_Concurrency\/AsyncSequence\/batch(clock:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/_Concurrency\/AsyncSequence\/deliver(to:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/_Concurrency\/AsyncSequence\/deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Delivery","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InvalidBatchBufferLimit","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/BufferDropReport"],"title":"Delivering","anchor":"Delivering"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination"},{"type":"text","text":" is a plain sink with one requirement, "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which is given"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a batch of records, oldest first. Delivering is a chain of operators over a tracker’s records:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch()"},{"type":"text","text":" gathers them into batches of 20, and every 30 seconds while any are pending, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:)"},{"type":"text","text":" makes a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Delivery"},{"type":"text","text":", which hands each batch to every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination. It holds a lazy unit of work, "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Delivery\/work"},{"type":"text","text":", that runs once you call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"execute()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each destination receives its batches in order, one at a time, from a buffer of its own, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"slow one delays only itself. A full buffer drops its oldest batch and reports it as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/BufferDropReport","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" on the delivery’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Delivery\/bufferDropReports","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which one task reads at a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"time, as every report stream does. When the tracker has a store, the delivery reads the dropped","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch’s records back for that destination once it catches up, and tells the store when each batch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has reached every destination.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What a destination receives is narrowed by modifiers: "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consent categories it serves, "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()"},{"type":"text","text":", and added to by "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/enriched(by:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which runs an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Enricher"},{"type":"text","text":" on the records that destination alone receives. "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/ConsoleDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"prints each event, and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps the newest records it receives for the app to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read, in a debug view or a test."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Logs, traces and servers have destinations in modules of their own, so an app links only the ones","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it uses: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LoggerDestination"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LoggingDestinations"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SpanEventDestination"},{"text":" in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TracingDestinations"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestinations"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["struct Uploader: Destination {","    func receive(_ batch: [EventRecord]) async {","        \/\/ Send the batch, and return once it is somewhere it won't be lost.","    }","}","","let inspector = try InMemoryDestination(capacity: 500)","let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records","    .batch(strategy: .count(20))","    .deliver(","        to: Uploader().accepting(.analytics).redactingSensitiveValues().droppingCallSite(),","        inspector","    )","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","await tracker.finish()","try await delivery.execute()","let received = inspector.events(of: SignedUp.self)  \/\/ [SignedUp(plan: \"pro\")]"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The umbrella guide on this area is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/destinations"]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Destinations"}],"externalID":"Destinations","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"Destinations"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where tracked events go: the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Destination"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol, the modifiers that narrow what a destination receives, and the delivery that hands it batches."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"references":{"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations/ConsoleDestination":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/ConsoleDestination","abstract":[{"text":"A destination that prints each event on a line of its own: its name, then the value.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/destinations\/consoledestination","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConsoleDestination","